<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine peso ends slightly up on low oil demand.</title>
<headline>Philippine peso ends slightly up on low oil demand.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Feb 17 -------------------------</p>
<p>* Central Bank buys about $60 million</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso was helped on Monday by low dollar demand from oil companies for the week, traders said.</p>
<p>The peso settled at its day-high of 26.344 in the last deal of the day after opening at 26.347. It closed at 26.345 last Friday.</p>
<p>Traders said oil firms indicated they will buy about $30 million this week versus more than $100 million last week.</p>
</text>
